            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Tamil for at present, then the Tamil for once in a while."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: பின்னர்",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "பின்னர் — piṉṉar — \"later on; afterwards\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "முதலில் நாங்கள் சாப்பிட்டோம், பின்னர் கடைக்குப் போனோம். mutalil nāṅkaḷ cāppiṭṭōm, piṉṉar kaṭaikkup pōṉōm. First we ate, and later on we went to the shop."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A more formal word for பிறகு."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "பின்னர் (piṉṉar) is native Dravidian: it is built on பின், \"back, what comes after\" (DEDR 4205)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
            }
          ]
        },
